      "has_children": false,
      "in_trash": false,
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "So Why Does This Matter? The GERD dispute highlights the fragility of transboundary water management in the Nile basin, with implications for regional water security and geopolitical stability. Sudan’s compromised water infrastructure and conflict add complexity. How Ethiopia’s unilateral dam operation affects downstream countries remains a critical risk for the region’s energy and water balance.",
              "link": null
            },
            "annotations": {
              "bold": false,
              "italic": false,
              "strikethrough": false,
              "underline": false,
              "code": false,
              "color": "default"
            },
            "plain_text": "So Why Does This Matter? The GERD dispute highlights the fragility of transboundary water management in the Nile basin, with implications for regional water security and geopolitical stability. Sudan’s compromised water infrastructure and conflict add complexity. How Ethiopia’s unilateral dam operation affects downstream countries remains a critical risk for the region’s energy and water balance.",
            "href": null
          }
        ],
        "icon": null,
        "color": "default"
      },
      "archived": false
